From: Andrzej Rogozynski <sellen@cs-lab.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] draw into a software shadow of the screen

set_video_mode() asks for an SDL_HWSURFACE screen.  Under SDL 1.2's
fbcon driver that surface is the mapped frame buffer itself, so every
step of a redraw (background, shaded panels, pieces, text) is visible
the moment it is written, and SDL_UpdateRects does nothing: the bowl,
the side panels and the menu flicker with half-drawn frames.  The
alpha-blended panels also read the frame buffer back, which is slow on
video memory and keeps each half-drawn state on screen longer.

Ask for SDL_SWSURFACE instead.  SDL then keeps the screen in RAM and
the game's own SDL_UpdateRects calls copy only finished areas to the
frame buffer (lbreakout2 does the same).

--- a/src/sdl.c
+++ b/src/sdl.c
@@ -908,7 +908,7 @@
     SDL_PixelFormat	*fmt;
 #endif
     int w, h;
-    int vflags = (fullscreen?SDL_FULLSCREEN:0) | SDL_HWSURFACE;
+    int vflags = (fullscreen?SDL_FULLSCREEN:0) | SDL_SWSURFACE;
 
     /* free old screen */
     if (sdl.screen) {
